From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:24:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/25] Add x86_64-unknown-plan9 (9front): target, std on
 9front's own libc

Linked by 9front's gcc port (x86_64-pc-plan9-gcc) against /amd64/lib.gcc/libc.a.
Threads are procs (rfork RFMEM) on stacks that are segments with gaps between
them (an overflow faults); main on such a stack through libgcc's
__plan9_mainstack; futex from the kernel's semaphores; thread-locals in a
privalloc slot; errors are the error strings. fs, env, process, net: not yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
